> But how does one prevent the hp augmentation? Can you just put 0's
> where it seems like the game is trying to add hps? Will it break
> anything?

You can replace the second parameter to healup() with 0, and then your
max HP will not increase.  If the first parameter is 0, then the
second parameter's value is irrelevant.
(Third and fourth parameters are boolean values, TRUE or FALSE, and
tell whether to cure sickness and blindness, respectively.)

> As far as corpse intrinsics, I imagine that trying to extract that
> feature from the game isn't even worth looking into, but I thought I'd
> ask anyway.

Corpse intrinsics are (mainly) defined in the huge array of monster
data, in src/monst.c; For example in the quivering blob -entry there's
the following line:
MR_SLEEP|MR_POISON, MR_POISON,
which means the blobs are resistant to sleep and poison, and eating
the corpse grants poison resistance. (But, as this is NetHack, there
are exceptions...)

The monst.c array field meanings you can see in include/permonst.h,
and the MR_* and other monster flags are in include/monflag.h

